INSERT INTO `pages` (`slug`, `content`) VALUES ('story', '{"heading":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Our story / Since 2006","ka":""},"title":{"en":"Old roots.\nNew rituals.","ka":""},"subtitle":{"en":"A Georgian point of view.\nFrom our vineyards to your table.","ka":""}},"cover":{"image":"/images/vineyard.webp","caption":{"en":"Kakheti, Georgia","ka":""}},"intro":{"eyebrow":{"en":"01 / The beginning","ka":""},"heading":{"en":"It started\nwith a place.","ka":""},"paragraph1":{"en":"In 2006, Giorgi Salakaia founded Badagoni in Zemo Khodasheni, in the heart of Kakheti. The ambition was clear: make Georgian wine that could express the full character of its place.","ka":""},"paragraph2":{"en":"Today, that idea guides everything we do. We work with native Georgian grape varieties, connecting an enduring winemaking heritage with contemporary research and knowledge.","ka":""}},"qvevri":{"image":"/images/cellar.webp","eyebrow":{"en":"02 / The craft","ka":""},"heading":{"en":"Of earth.\nOf time.","ka":""},"paragraph1":{"en":"At Alaverdi Monastery, wine is part of a living heritage. Badagoni helped restore the historic cellar in 2006, supporting the continuation of its winemaking tradition.","ka":""},"paragraph2":{"en":"Our qvevri wines are made in clay vessels buried in the earth, connecting each harvest to generations of Georgian craft.","ka":""}},"winery":{"eyebrow":{"en":"03 / The winery","ka":""},"heading":{"en":"Inside\nour winery.","ka":""},"paragraph1":{"en":"In Zemo Khodasheni, Kakheti, our winery brings Georgian grapes together with Italian winemaking technology. Fermentation takes place in stainless steel tanks, while selected wines mature in American, French and Slovenian oak.","ka":""},"paragraph2":{"en":"Laboratory analysis begins with the soil and continues throughout winemaking. Our own laboratory and Enosis Meraviglia in Italy provide the research and testing behind each bottle.","ka":""}},"science":{"eyebrow":{"en":"04 / The perspective","ka":""},"heading":{"en":"Tradition has\na future.","ka":""},"paragraph":{"en":"Our collaboration with oenologist Dr. Donato Lanati and the Enosis Meraviglia research centre brings a scientific perspective to the vineyard and the cellar. The aim is always the same: allow each Georgian variety to speak clearly.","ka":""}}}');
